DESCRIPTION:I’ve invited George Miloshevich to talk about this work: htt
 ps://arxiv.org/pdf/2510.00282<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook
 .com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Farxiv.org%2Fpdf%2F2510.00282&data=05%7C02%7Crzha
 ngbq%40gatech.edu%7C1d8fc0fe457e4bf8cdd708de0f30b364%7C482198bbae7b4b258
 b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638964899003480113%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJ
 FbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCI
 sIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=B2dlczxkS%2FGoJ3JnIFwBLuLaERv4cmZVG
 0VRZnC2aOM%3D&reserved=0> This is a talk jointly for HighZ FIC and CHaRM
 NET MMICC.\n\nHere is the link:\nYanrui Ma is inviting you to a schedule
 d Zoom meeting.\nJoin Zoom Meeting\nhttps://msu.zoom.us/j/91862205096<ht
 tps://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fmsu.zoom
 .us%2Fj%2F91862205096&data=05%7C02%7Crzhangbq%40gatech.edu%7C1d8fc0fe457
 e4bf8cdd708de0f30b364%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C63896
 4899003506260%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLj
 AuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&
 sdata=lCxGesaVwIGcvCFnh7bIaWFfEQXQGZbFJK78oUhVL4g%3D&reserved=0>\n\nMeet
 ing ID: 918 6220 5096\n\nUpdate with his title and abstract below:\n\nTi
 tle: Kinetic modelling of magnetosheath turbulence: machine learning clo
 sure and dissipation\n\nAbstract:\nThe dynamics of decaying turbulence i
 n the magnetosheath is investigated using fully kinetic PIC simulations 
 with ECsim. We find a rather broad range of electron beta values. Furthe
 rmore\, anisotropies are shown to be well bounded by whistler and fireho
 se instabilities in both 2D3V and 3D3V simulations with mean pressure-st
 rain values enhanced near the instability thresholds. From these simulat
 ions\, we derive a data-driven five-moment closure with an improved gene
 ralized Ohm’s law\, where the pressure tensor is trained directly on ful
 ly kinetic simulations. We find that finite Larmor radius (FLR) effects 
 are reproduced by a non-local formulation\, which outperforms traditiona
 l double adiabatic closures. This formulation demonstrates generalizatio
 n capability on more physically accurate\, high-particles-per-cell kinet
 ic runs\, successfully recovering key energy-transfer signatures such as
  the statistics of pressure-strain interactions. Building on this result
 \, we implement the data-driven electron closure in a hybrid PIC code.\n
 \nhttps://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00282<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.ou
 tlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Farxiv.org%2Fabs%2F2510.00282&data=05%7C02%7
 Crzhangbq%40gatech.edu%7C1d8fc0fe457e4bf8cdd708de0f30b364%7C482198bbae7b
 4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638964899003528492%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3
 d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTW
 FpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=kqj9BUAxvKoADIHRvIqTh84vngvM3x
 US%2Btc3gctzSYg%3D&reserved=0>\n\n
