CREATED:20260125T225039Z
DESCRIPTION:We will host Jingwei Hu (University of Washington\, https://
 jingweihu-math.github.io/webpage/<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.out
 look.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fjingweihu-math.github.io%2Fwebpage%2F&data=0
 5%7C02%7Crzhangbq%40gatech.edu%7C24fa6ca048bc421cec7e08ddd14b1cd1%7C4821
 98bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638896842736552676%7CUnknown%7CTW
 FpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIk
 FOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=y6kAnpdo6wC0EiU9xlzEfv
 XZxlxw3W9I7mgHqQBRPek%3D&reserved=0>) as a DDPS seminar speaker. Hope to
  see you many of you at the seminar:\n\n\nStructure-Preserving Particle 
 Method for Collisional Plasmas\n\nJingwei Hu\n\nUniversity of Washington
 \n\nFriday\, August 15\, 2025\n10:00 AM\nWebEx\n\n\nAbstract:  The Vlaso
 v-Maxwell-Landau equation is often regarded as a first-principles physic
 s model for plasmas. In this talk\, we introduce a novel particle method
  for this equation\, which collectively models particle transport\, elec
 tromagnetic field effects\, and Coulomb collisions. The method arises fr
 om a regularization of the variational formulation of the Landau collisi
 on operator\, leading to a discretization that conserves mass\, momentum
 \, and energy\, as well as dissipates the entropy. The collisional effec
 ts appear as a fully deterministic effective force\, which can be natura
 lly coupled with the classical particle-in-cell (PIC) method. We validat
 e the method on several plasma benchmark tests\, including collisional L
 andau damping\, two-stream instability\, and Weibel instability.\n\n\nBi
 o: Jingwei Hu is a Professor in the Department of Applied Mathematics at
  the University of Washington. She also holds an adjunct professorship i
 n the William E. Boeing Department of Aeronautics & Astronautics. Dr. Hu
  earned her Ph.D. from the University of Wisconsin-Madison in 2011 and w
 as a postdoctoral fellow at the University of Texas at Austin from 2011 
 to 2014. Prior to joining UW in 2021\, she held positions as an Assistan
 t and later as an Associate Professor at Purdue University. Her research
  primarily focuses on developing efficient\, structure-preserving numeri
 cal methods for multiscale kinetic equations applied to various science 
 and engineering fields.\n\n\n📚 DDPS seminar is organized by libROM team
  ( www.librom.net<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=ht
 tp%3A%2F%2Fwww.librom.net%2F&data=05%7C02%7Crzhangbq%40gatech.edu%7C24fa
 6ca048bc421cec7e08ddd14b1cd1%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%
 7C638896842736580560%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlY
