DESCRIPTION:We will host Raphaël Pestourie (Georgia Tech\, https://www.r
 aphaelpestourie.com/<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url
 =https%3A%2F%2Fwww.raphaelpestourie.com%2F&data=05%7C02%7Crzhangbq%40gat
 ech.edu%7Ca5bc2f7e99ee4022f8b708ddbddd37b7%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32f
 aa083%7C1%7C0%7C638875479997140566%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hc
 GkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyf
 Q%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=fk1kcH3AtqxIlvxS6Zu4W1izqNzM%2BtpifG2vkBJCRSc
 %3D&reserved=0>) as a DDPS seminar speaker. Hope to see you many of you 
 at the seminar:\n\n\nInput-space Scientific machine learning for PDE-con
 strained optimization of geometries\n\nRaphaël Pestourie\n\nGeorgia Tech
 \n\nFriday\, July 11\, 2025\n10:00 AM\nWebEx\n\n\nAbstract:  In engineer
 ing design\, machine learning (ML) can enhance both the simulation and o
 ptimization of properties governed by partial differential equations (PD
 Es). However\, many scientific ML approaches focus on learning the PDE s
 olution itself–requiring the model to relearn physical laws already enco
 ded in the PDEs used to generate the data. In this talk\, we will presen
 t an alternative perspective: input-space scientific machine learning (S
 ciML). These methods model the input space of a PDE solver\, leaving the
  physics to the numerical solver. We will introduce Physics-Enhanced Dee
 p Surrogates (PEDS)\, an input-space SciML model that accelerates the si
 mulation of PDE-driven properties. We will also present a ML-enhanced op
 timization technique called HiLAB that enables efficient exploration of 
 high-dimensional design spaces for PDE-constrained optimization. We will
  demonstrate these methods on benchmark PDE problems and show experiment
 al validation of HiLAB in the context of nanophotonic metasurface design
 .\n\nBio: Raphaël Pestourie earned his Ph.D. in Applied Mathematics and 
 an AM in Statistics from Harvard University in 2020. Prior to Georgia Te
 ch\, he was a postdoctoral associate at MIT Mathematics\, where he worke
 d closely with the MIT-IBM Watson AI Lab. Raphaël’s research focuses on 
 scientific machine learning at the intersection of applied mathematics a
 nd machine learning and inverse design via scientific machine learning a
 nd large-scale electromagnetic design.\n\n\n📚 DDPS seminar is organized
  by libROM team ( www.librom.net<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outl
 ook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.librom.net%2F&data=05%7C02%7Crzhangbq%40ga
 tech.edu%7Ca5bc2f7e99ee4022f8b708ddbddd37b7%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32
 faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638875479997173124%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1h
 cGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoy
 fQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=VC4879x%2B4KAFVMymiW5U8lAdlqX7FIRzunNgrlBDIP
 8%3D&reserved=0> ).\n🗓️ DDPS seminar schedule: https://www.librom.net/d
