DESCRIPTION:\nSmarter Particles for Smarter Plasma Simulations: A Moment
 -Enhanced PIC Framework\nMandela Quashie\nThursday\, May 29\, 2025\n10:0
 0AM – 11:00AM PST\nLVOC B6527 R100 (Hybrid<https://nam12.safelinks.prote
 ction.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fllnlfed.webex.com%2Fllnlfed%2Fj.php
 %3FMTID%3Dmc503956b09e7640ca49daa6fc0e5d197&data=05%7C02%7Crzhangbq%40ga
 tech.edu%7C22beac8394b740ab9af108dd9e6d2327%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32
 faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638840913849567256%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1h
 cGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoy
 fQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=sUh6PsX95KZbMZ5oBbmLv%2BLa6HIKoHvaZfJl0dtiic
 c%3D&reserved=0>)\n\n\nABSTRACT\n\nThe Vlasov–Poisson system is a corner
 stone in modeling collisionless plasmas\, capturing how self-consistent 
 electric fields evolve from particle dynamics. However\, its infinite-di
 mensional structure poses significant challenges for simulation—especial
 ly when accuracy\, efficiency\, and fidelity to physical laws are crucia
 l. Traditional Particle-in-Cell (PIC) methods\, while widely used\, ofte
 n require large numbers of particles and suffer from noise and poor reso
 lution in sparsely sampled regions of phase space.\n\nIn this talk\, I p
 resent a moment-enhanced PIC method that enriches each simulation partic
 le with local moment data—such as density\, momentum\, and higher-order 
 derivatives. This added structure enables a more accurate representation
  of the distribution function with fewer particles. The approach is grou
 nded in a Poisson bracket formulation inspired by Scovel–Weinstein reduc
 tion\, leading to a finite-dimensional model that retains the Hamiltonia
 n structure of the original Vlasov dynamics.\n\nNumerical results for th
 e 1D Vlasov–Poisson system show improved stability\, reduced noise\, and
  better conservation of physical invariants such as energy and momentum.
  This framework paves the way for efficient\, structure-preserving kinet
 ic solvers in plasma physics and beyond.\n\n\nTechnical Contact: Youngso
 o Choi | 925.422.0217| choi15@llnl.gov<mailto:choi15@llnl.gov>\nAdminist
 rative Contact: Esmeralda Gonzalez | 925.424.3745 | gonzalez134@llnl.gov
 <mailto:gonzalez134@llnl.gov>\n\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-
