BEGIN:VEVENT
ATTENDEE;CN="Choi, Youngsoo";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="choi15@llnl.gov";P
 ARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;ROLE=CHAIR:mailto:choi15@llnl.gov
ATTENDEE;CN="Data Driven Physics Simulation";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="dd
 ps@llnl.gov";ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT:mailto:ddps@llnl.gov
ATTENDEE;CN="Johannes Brandstetter";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="brandstette
 r@ml.jku.at";ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT:mailto:brandstetter@ml.jku.at
CREATED:20260125T225041Z
DESCRIPTION:We will host Johannes Brandstetter (Johannes Kepler Universi
 ty\, https://brandstetter-johannes.github.io/) as a DDPS seminar speaker
 . Hope to see you many of you at the seminar:\n\n\nThe next wave of scie
 ntific breakthroughs is in the latent space\n\nJohannes Brandstetter\n\n
 Johannes Kepler University\n\nFriday\, May 2\, 2025\n10:00 AM\nWebEx\n\n
 \nAbstract: In the era of scaling and LLMs\, one gets notoriously confro
 nted with the question of where we stand with applicability of such powe
 rful techniques within scientific or engineering domains. The discussion
  starts by reiterating on recent triumphs in weather and climate modelin
 g\, making connections to computer vision\, physics-informed learning an
 d neural operators. Secondly\, we discuss challenges and conceptual barr
 iers which need to be overcome for the next wave of disruption in scienc
 e and engineering. We showcase recent breakthroughs in multi-physics mod
 eling\, molecular dynamics\, computational fluid dynamics\, nuclear fusi
 on and related fields.\n\nBio: Johannes Brandstetter did his PhD studyin
 g Higgs boson decays at the CMS experiment at the Large Hadron Collider 
 at CERN. In 2018\, he joined Sepp Hochreiter’s group in Linz\, Austria. 
 In 2021\, he became ELLIS PostDoc at Max Welling’s lab at the University
  of Amsterdam\, before joining the newly founded Microsoft Lab in Amster
 dam. During his time at Microsoft Research\, Johannes was working on sca
 ling up of AI driven physics surrogates\, most notably for weather and c
 limate simulations. In October 2023\, Johannes Brandstetter moved back t
 o Austria and started a new group “AI for data-driven simulations” at th
 e Institute of Machine Learning at the Johannes Kepler University (JKU) 
 in Linz. Additionally\, in 2024 Johannes was Chief Researcher at NXAI Gm
 bH. Recently\, Johannes co-founded Emmi AI where he is currently is the 
 Chief Scientist.\n\n📚 DDPS seminar is organized by libROM team ( www.li
 brom.net<http://www.librom.net> ).\n🗓️ DDPS seminar schedule: https://w
 ww.librom.net/ddps.html<https://www.youtube.com/redirect?event=video_des
 cription&redir_token=QUFFLUhqblRkS256NDFhdjRyNHpRRFYwSm5jT0t0MVNvZ3xBQ3J
 tc0treERKS1BuSkhPd3FHaXFqRDZPUnZtRjh1b01WcjJuczBSZFA1aGRranNtOVNFNlpONmx
 HSkRHLUZEeVA5Y24wVXRHRi1wdGdDT3E5RlFneHFVdUpNTk1KeEIwNjMzLTBTVjZueDRodXp
 0c2VLWTZDUQ&q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.librom.net%2Fddps.html&v=uksMn36aecg>\n
 💻 LLNL News: https://www.llnl.gov/news<https://www.youtube.com/redirect?
 event=video_description&redir_token=QUFFLUhqa2RhQlRlU3N0QThpOFhfeFJhclpS
 d0RRRkFGd3xBQ3Jtc0trdlZna1FQcmQtVG1CQ3VOUVoxekpPalR4ZlFUdjRXSmtJSEFmM3Na
