 __\nFrom: Faculty <faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:faculty-bounces@
 cc.gatech.edu>> On Behalf Of Sarkar\, Vivek\nSent: Wednesday\, February 
 19\, 2025 1:53 PM\nTo: Faculty@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Faculty@cc.gatech.ed
 u>\; Staff@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Staff@cc.gatech.edu>\; phd-coc-official@
 cc.gatech.edu<mailto:phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; ms-coc-official@c
 c.gatech.edu<mailto:ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; cocadvisoryboard@cc
 .gatech.edu<mailto:cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu>\nSubject: [Faculty] D
 ean's Dispatch – new committees for changing times\, kudos\n\nDear GT Co
 mputing community\,\n\nMany things are changing right now\, sometimes on
  a daily basis.  I know this can be stressful for everyone.  As I mentio
 ned during the listening sessions\, our greatest strength is our people.
  We are lucky to have talented\, dedicated individuals who make ours a t
 ruly vibrant community.  This is very much a time for all of us to come 
 together and express kindness and compassion for everyone\, especially t
 hose who are the most vulnerable.  And be sure to extend kindness to you
 rself as well. No matter what the future brings\, we will face it togeth
 er as a community.\n\nTo keep communication channels active\, I am also 
 scheduling weekly virtual office hours with the Dean for all CoC faculty
 \, staff\, and students who would like to discuss any aspect of recent e
 vents and their potential impacts.  These will be held during 11:30am - 
 12:30pm on Thursdays\, starting tomorrow (Feb 20th).  Please look out fo
 r a calendar invitation and contact Cynthia Bryant (cebryant@cc.gatech.e
 du<mailto:cebryant@cc.gatech.edu>) if you don’t see one.\n\nIn addition 
 to the listening sessions\, I very much appreciated meeting with our col
 lege advisory board members last Friday.  We are lucky to have such a ta
 lented and experienced group of experts on our advisory board who care d
 eeply about our college and are ready to share their advice and support 
 in every way that they can.  It was very helpful to hear their perspecti
 ves\, and I look forward to further discussions during our upcoming advi
 sory board meeting on April 3-4.\n\nIn other news\, I am pleased to anno
 unce that Melinda McDaniel is the new interim Associate Chair of the Sch
 ool of Computing Instruction. Melinda is a GT alumna and has a decade of
  experience teaching our undergraduates --- we are lucky to have her in 
 this leadership position.  Many thanks to Melinda for stepping up this i
 mportant role for SCI and the college!\n\nI'd also like to share updates
  on the two committees mentioned in last week's dispatch.  Both committe
 es will welcome getting input from all of you\, of course.\n\nCoC Contin
 gency Planning Committee\nThis committee includes representation from fa
 culty\, staff\, and students. Its scope will include staying abreast of 
 recent developments\, identifying scenarios that need contingency planni
 ng\, and recommending contingency efforts for those scenarios.  It inclu
 des the following members:\n\n  *   Greg Eisenhauer (Senior Research Sci
 entist\, SCS)\n  *   Ada Gavrilovska (Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Neha Kumar
  (Associate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Kim Macleod (Associate Director of En
 terprise Services\, TSO)\n  *   Melinda McDaniel (Senior Lecturer\, SCI)
 \n  *   Peter Swire (J.Z. Liang Professor\, SCP and Scheller)\n  *   Xiu
 wei Zhang (J.Z. Liang Early-Career Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n\nWe are 
 still waiting on confirming the student member of this committee and wil
 l announce their name when it is confirmed.\n\nCoC Task Force on New Str
 ategies for Funding Computing Research\nThis task force will be in charg
 e of thinking strategically about exploring new ways to fund the researc
 h of CoC faculty\, especially in areas that are vulnerable to loss of fu
 nding. It includes the following members:\n\n  *   Carlos Batist (Assist
 ant Director - Financial Operations\, SCS)\n  *   Tom Conte (Associate D
 ean for Research\, CoC\; and\, Professor\, SCS & ECE - Task Force Lead)\
 n  *   Alberto Dainotti (Associate Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Munmun De Cho
 udhury (Associate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Rich DeMillo (Charlotte B. and 
 Roger C. Warren Professor of Computing\, SCP)\n  *   Kristine Haskett (E
 xecutive Director Foundation Relations\, GT Office of Development)\n  * 
   Josiah Hester (Catherine M. and James E. Allchin Early Career Associat
 e Professor\, IC)\n  *   Tamara Pearson (Senior Director\, Constellation
 s Center\, CoC)\n  *   Chao Zhang (Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n  *   Jas
 on Zwang (Senior Director\, Development\, CoC)\n\nFinally\, I have kudos
  to share for members of our community\, as always:\n\n  *   Our student
  Competitive Programming team has dominated in recent competitions.\n   
   *   Nearly 100 Tech students took part in the Meta Hacker Cup\, with s
 ix students making it to the third round. Ph.D. candidate Sunghyeong Jo 
 placed 8th in the third round and was one of 500 to make it to the final
  round\, where he placed 13th.\n     *   At the International Collegiate
  Programming Contest (ICPC) regionals\, Georgia Tech teams secured four 
 of the top 10 spots. The top Georgia Tech team of Weiyu Chen\, Kevin Sha
 n\, and Xieting Chu solved all 13 problems\, placing second in the regio
 n and third nationally. Congratulations to all of the team members and t
 o Abrahim Ladha (SCI)\, their faculty advisor. Well done!\n\n  *   Our e
 ntrepreneurial capstone course has more than doubled in size since we la
 unched it in 2023\, with a current enrollment of 126 students. In respon
 se\, the College is expanding its course sections and deepening our rela
 tionship with CREATE-X\, the Institute’s entrepreneurship education init
 iative.  See the related story<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outloo
 k.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-part
 nership-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7C
 rzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C9c649fd9135c483a6dd108dde6666273%7
 C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638920049636259111%7CUnknown
 %7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zM
 iIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=K%2B5wDsF%2BL%2BY
 ecMtpREeIP6%2Bt8wfzDjGESUFaBg3xf5k%3D&reserved=0> for details.\n\nThat’s
  all for this week.  Please stay warm!\n\nBest regards\,\n\nVivek\n\nPS 
 -- I’d like to remind everyone that our institute’s Spring Compliance Tr
 aining is under way\, and that everyone in the college (including studen
 t employees) must complete it by February 28. I have completed it myself
  and can attest that it’s not too cumbersome … and it was interesting to
  see a module there related to GenAI!\n\nStudent programming team: https
 ://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/competitive-programming-team-excels-major-comp
 etitions<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F
 %2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcompetitive-programming-team-excels-major-
 competitions&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C9c649f
 d9135c483a6dd108dde6666273%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C
 638920049636281041%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiO
 iIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7
 C%7C&sdata=nd0X1674KdTY5QrFYaevIo1rQwaao1%2FYLcKmq7DldAs%3D&reserved=0>\
 n\nExpanding its course selections and deepening our relationship with C
 REATE-X: https://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/college-expands-partnership-crea
 te-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum<https://nam12.safelinks.pro
 tection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcolleg
 e-expands-partnership-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&d
 ata=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C9c649fd9135c483a6dd1
 08dde6666273%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C63892004963630
 0622%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCI
 sIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=dtE
 jwEmehn%2Fhz6hWlMdedVj80bIYbXpEAI1Hh1sumoA%3D&reserved=0>\n\n\nVivek Sar
 kar<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fvsa
 rkar.cc.gatech.edu%2F&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com
 %7C9c649fd9135c483a6dd108dde6666273%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7
 C1%7C0%7C638920049636317481%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRy
 dWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D
 %7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=1uwrQgzOnoBHgrE4w6nUfJitin%2FfDnpv5cnZuigzpFY%3D&res
 erved=0>\nJohn P. Imlay Jr. Dean\, College of Computing\nGeorgia Institu
 te of Technology\nEA: Cynthia Bryant\, cebryant@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:ceb
 ryant@cc.gatech.edu>\, 404-385-5661\n\n\n\nMy work hours might differ fr
 om yours\, so please don’t feel obligated to respond to my evening/weeke
 nd/holiday emails until you are back at work.\n\n[cid:image001.jpg@01DB8
 2E3.590FB3F0]\n\n
