 _____________________________________\nFrom: Faculty <faculty-bounces@cc
 .gatech.edu<mailto:faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu>> On Behalf Of Sarkar\,
  Vivek\nSent: Wednesday\, February 19\, 2025 1:53 PM\nTo: Faculty@cc.gat
 ech.edu<mailto:Faculty@cc.gatech.edu>\; Staff@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Staff
 @cc.gatech.edu>\; phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:phd-coc-official
 @cc.gatech.edu>\; ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:ms-coc-official@c
 c.gatech.edu>\; cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cocadvisoryboard@c
 c.gatech.edu>\nSubject: [Faculty] Dean's Dispatch – new committees for c
 hanging times\, kudos\n\nDear GT Computing community\,\n\nMany things ar
 e changing right now\, sometimes on a daily basis.  I know this can be s
 tressful for everyone.  As I mentioned during the listening sessions\, o
 ur greatest strength is our people. We are lucky to have talented\, dedi
 cated individuals who make ours a truly vibrant community.  This is very
  much a time for all of us to come together and express kindness and com
 passion for everyone\, especially those who are the most vulnerable.  An
 d be sure to extend kindness to yourself as well. No matter what the fut
 ure brings\, we will face it together as a community.\n\nTo keep communi
 cation channels active\, I am also scheduling weekly virtual office hour
 s with the Dean for all CoC faculty\, staff\, and students who would lik
 e to discuss any aspect of recent events and their potential impacts.  T
 hese will be held during 11:30am - 12:30pm on Thursdays\, starting tomor
 row (Feb 20th).  Please look out for a calendar invitation and contact C
 ynthia Bryant (cebryant@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cebryant@cc.gatech.edu>) if
  you don’t see one.\n\nIn addition to the listening sessions\, I very mu
 ch appreciated meeting with our college advisory board members last Frid
 ay.  We are lucky to have such a talented and experienced group of exper
 ts on our advisory board who care deeply about our college and are ready
  to share their advice and support in every way that they can.  It was v
 ery helpful to hear their perspectives\, and I look forward to further d
 iscussions during our upcoming advisory board meeting on April 3-4.\n\nI
 n other news\, I am pleased to announce that Melinda McDaniel is the new
  interim Associate Chair of the School of Computing Instruction. Melinda
  is a GT alumna and has a decade of experience teaching our undergraduat
 es --- we are lucky to have her in this leadership position.  Many thank
 s to Melinda for stepping up this important role for SCI and the college
 !\n\nI'd also like to share updates on the two committees mentioned in l
 ast week's dispatch.  Both committees will welcome getting input from al
 l of you\, of course.\n\nCoC Contingency Planning Committee\nThis commit
 tee includes representation from faculty\, staff\, and students. Its sco
 pe will include staying abreast of recent developments\, identifying sce
 narios that need contingency planning\, and recommending contingency eff
 orts for those scenarios.  It includes the following members:\n\n  *   G
 reg Eisenhauer (Senior Research Scientist\, SCS)\n  *   Ada Gavrilovska 
 (Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Neha Kumar (Associate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Ki
 m Macleod (Associate Director of Enterprise Services\, TSO)\n  *   Melin
 da McDaniel (Senior Lecturer\, SCI)\n  *   Peter Swire (J.Z. Liang Profe
 ssor\, SCP and Scheller)\n  *   Xiuwei Zhang (J.Z. Liang Early-Career As
 sistant Professor\, CSE)\n\nWe are still waiting on confirming the stude
 nt member of this committee and will announce their name when it is conf
 irmed.\n\nCoC Task Force on New Strategies for Funding Computing Researc
 h\nThis task force will be in charge of thinking strategically about exp
 loring new ways to fund the research of CoC faculty\, especially in area
 s that are vulnerable to loss of funding. It includes the following memb
 ers:\n\n  *   Carlos Batist (Assistant Director - Financial Operations\,
  SCS)\n  *   Tom Conte (Associate Dean for Research\, CoC\; and\, Profes
 sor\, SCS & ECE - Task Force Lead)\n  *   Alberto Dainotti (Associate Pr
 ofessor\, SCS)\n  *   Munmun De Choudhury (Associate Professor\, IC)\n  
 *   Rich DeMillo (Charlotte B. and Roger C. Warren Professor of Computin
 g\, SCP)\n  *   Kristine Haskett (Executive Director Foundation Relation
 s\, GT Office of Development)\n  *   Josiah Hester (Catherine M. and Jam
 es E. Allchin Early Career Associate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Tamara Pears
 on (Senior Director\, Constellations Center\, CoC)\n  *   Chao Zhang (As
 sistant Professor\, CSE)\n  *   Jason Zwang (Senior Director\, Developme
 nt\, CoC)\n\nFinally\, I have kudos to share for members of our communit
 y\, as always:\n\n  *   Our student Competitive Programming team has dom
 inated in recent competitions.\n     *   Nearly 100 Tech students took p
 art in the Meta Hacker Cup\, with six students making it to the third ro
 und. Ph.D. candidate Sunghyeong Jo placed 8th in the third round and was
  one of 500 to make it to the final round\, where he placed 13th.\n     
 *   At the International Collegiate Programming Contest (ICPC) regionals
 \, Georgia Tech teams secured four of the top 10 spots. The top Georgia 
 Tech team of Weiyu Chen\, Kevin Shan\, and Xieting Chu solved all 13 pro
 blems\, placing second in the region and third nationally. Congratulatio
 ns to all of the team members and to Abrahim Ladha (SCI)\, their faculty
  advisor. Well done!\n\n  *   Our entrepreneurial capstone course has mo
 re than doubled in size since we launched it in 2023\, with a current en
 rollment of 126 students. In response\, the College is expanding its cou
 rse sections and deepening our relationship with CREATE-X\, the Institut
 e’s entrepreneurship education initiative.  See the related story<https:
 //nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatec
 h.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-partnership-create-x-double-down-entrepre
 neurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7
 C7c2d5b0f5e334e896e6308ddeae2af3d%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1
 %7C0%7C638924981535817791%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydW
 UsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7
 C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=hYR0b2E6aiRpwRkSHCPbc2XJbofhwGR71Y9DHBfbkPQ%3D&reserve
 d=0> for details.\n\nThat’s all for this week.  Please stay warm!\n\nBes
 t regards\,\n\nVivek\n\nPS -- I’d like to remind everyone that our insti
 tute’s Spring Compliance Training is under way\, and that everyone in th
 e college (including student employees) must complete it by February 28.
  I have completed it myself and can attest that it’s not too cumbersome 
 … and it was interesting to see a module there related to GenAI!\n\nStud
 ent programming team: https://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/competitive-program
 ming-team-excels-major-competitions<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.o
 utlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcompetitive-pro
 gramming-team-excels-major-competitions&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvau
 lt.onmicrosoft.com%7C7c2d5b0f5e334e896e6308ddeae2af3d%7C482198bbae7b4b25
 8b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638924981535832097%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8ey
 JFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbC
 IsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=WryPfWUgONaiKtkpW52u%2B1j6ez0Bl55l
 tQ0hIRUHzcs%3D&reserved=0>\n\nExpanding its course selections and deepen
 ing our relationship with CREATE-X: https://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/colle
 ge-expands-partnership-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum<
 https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc
 .gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-partnership-create-x-double-down-en
 trepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft
 .com%7C7c2d5b0f5e334e896e6308ddeae2af3d%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa0
 83%7C1%7C0%7C638924981535846986%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGki
 OnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3
 D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=XoAg2xboCwMMBYcMvz%2B2kunANNcB5iHGfR5fqAqNQjw%3D
 &reserved=0>\n\n\nVivek Sarkar<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outloo
 k.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fvsarkar.cc.gatech.edu%2F&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang66
 2%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C7c2d5b0f5e334e896e6308ddeae2af3d%7C482198b
 bae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638924981535862690%7CUnknown%7CTWFpb
 GZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOI
 joiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=0WuuzQ9mDgZJDhvgMAIFcEB9I
 N5L88f5%2FE52SUWm79A%3D&reserved=0>\nJohn P. Imlay Jr. Dean\, College of
  Computing\nGeorgia Institute of Technology\nEA: Cynthia Bryant\, cebrya
 nt@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cebryant@cc.gatech.edu>\, 404-385-5661\n\n\n\nMy
  work hours might differ from yours\, so please don’t feel obligated to 
 respond to my evening/weekend/holiday emails until you are back at work.
