 _________________________________________________________________\nFrom:
  Faculty <faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:faculty-bounces@cc.gatech
 .edu>> On Behalf Of Sarkar\, Vivek\nSent: Wednesday\, February 19\, 2025
  1:53 PM\nTo: Faculty@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Faculty@cc.gatech.edu>\; Staf
 f@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Staff@cc.gatech.edu>\; phd-coc-official@cc.gatech
 .edu<mailto:phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.
 edu<mailto:ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.e
 du<mailto:cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu>\nSubject: [Faculty] Dean's Dis
 patch – new committees for changing times\, kudos\n\nDear GT Computing c
 ommunity\,\n\nMany things are changing right now\, sometimes on a daily 
 basis.  I know this can be stressful for everyone.  As I mentioned durin
 g the listening sessions\, our greatest strength is our people. We are l
 ucky to have talented\, dedicated individuals who make ours a truly vibr
 ant community.  This is very much a time for all of us to come together 
 and express kindness and compassion for everyone\, especially those who 
 are the most vulnerable.  And be sure to extend kindness to yourself as 
 well. No matter what the future brings\, we will face it together as a c
 ommunity.\n\nTo keep communication channels active\, I am also schedulin
 g weekly virtual office hours with the Dean for all CoC faculty\, staff\
 , and students who would like to discuss any aspect of recent events and
  their potential impacts.  These will be held during 11:30am - 12:30pm o
 n Thursdays\, starting tomorrow (Feb 20th).  Please look out for a calen
 dar invitation and contact Cynthia Bryant (cebryant@cc.gatech.edu<mailto
 :cebryant@cc.gatech.edu>) if you don’t see one.\n\nIn addition to the li
 stening sessions\, I very much appreciated meeting with our college advi
 sory board members last Friday.  We are lucky to have such a talented an
 d experienced group of experts on our advisory board who care deeply abo
 ut our college and are ready to share their advice and support in every 
 way that they can.  It was very helpful to hear their perspectives\, and
  I look forward to further discussions during our upcoming advisory boar
 d meeting on April 3-4.\n\nIn other news\, I am pleased to announce that
  Melinda McDaniel is the new interim Associate Chair of the School of Co
 mputing Instruction. Melinda is a GT alumna and has a decade of experien
 ce teaching our undergraduates --- we are lucky to have her in this lead
 ership position.  Many thanks to Melinda for stepping up this important 
 role for SCI and the college!\n\nI'd also like to share updates on the t
 wo committees mentioned in last week's dispatch.  Both committees will w
 elcome getting input from all of you\, of course.\n\nCoC Contingency Pla
 nning Committee\nThis committee includes representation from faculty\, s
 taff\, and students. Its scope will include staying abreast of recent de
 velopments\, identifying scenarios that need contingency planning\, and 
 recommending contingency efforts for those scenarios.  It includes the f
 ollowing members:\n\n  *   Greg Eisenhauer (Senior Research Scientist\, 
 SCS)\n  *   Ada Gavrilovska (Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Neha Kumar (Associa
 te Professor\, IC)\n  *   Kim Macleod (Associate Director of Enterprise 
 Services\, TSO)\n  *   Melinda McDaniel (Senior Lecturer\, SCI)\n  *   P
 eter Swire (J.Z. Liang Professor\, SCP and Scheller)\n  *   Xiuwei Zhang
  (J.Z. Liang Early-Career Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n\nWe are still wai
 ting on confirming the student member of this committee and will announc
 e their name when it is confirmed.\n\nCoC Task Force on New Strategies f
 or Funding Computing Research\nThis task force will be in charge of thin
 king strategically about exploring new ways to fund the research of CoC 
 faculty\, especially in areas that are vulnerable to loss of funding. It
  includes the following members:\n\n  *   Carlos Batist (Assistant Direc
 tor - Financial Operations\, SCS)\n  *   Tom Conte (Associate Dean for R
 esearch\, CoC\; and\, Professor\, SCS & ECE - Task Force Lead)\n  *   Al
 berto Dainotti (Associate Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Munmun De Choudhury (A
 ssociate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Rich DeMillo (Charlotte B. and Roger C. 
 Warren Professor of Computing\, SCP)\n  *   Kristine Haskett (Executive 
 Director Foundation Relations\, GT Office of Development)\n  *   Josiah 
 Hester (Catherine M. and James E. Allchin Early Career Associate Profess
 or\, IC)\n  *   Tamara Pearson (Senior Director\, Constellations Center\
 , CoC)\n  *   Chao Zhang (Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n  *   Jason Zwang 
 (Senior Director\, Development\, CoC)\n\nFinally\, I have kudos to share
  for members of our community\, as always:\n\n  *   Our student Competit
 ive Programming team has dominated in recent competitions.\n     *   Nea
 rly 100 Tech students took part in the Meta Hacker Cup\, with six studen
 ts making it to the third round. Ph.D. candidate Sunghyeong Jo placed 8t
 h in the third round and was one of 500 to make it to the final round\, 
 where he placed 13th.\n     *   At the International Collegiate Programm
 ing Contest (ICPC) regionals\, Georgia Tech teams secured four of the to
 p 10 spots. The top Georgia Tech team of Weiyu Chen\, Kevin Shan\, and X
 ieting Chu solved all 13 problems\, placing second in the region and thi
 rd nationally. Congratulations to all of the team members and to Abrahim
  Ladha (SCI)\, their faculty advisor. Well done!\n\n  *   Our entreprene
 urial capstone course has more than doubled in size since we launched it
  in 2023\, with a current enrollment of 126 students. In response\, the 
 College is expanding its course sections and deepening our relationship 
 with CREATE-X\, the Institute’s entrepreneurship education initiative.  
 See the related story<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?ur
 l=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-partnership-c
 reate-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662
 %40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C5974ea5c532441d76ff308ddf53e3f29%7C482198bb
 ae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638936369928689471%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbG
 Zsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIj
 oiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=rhoGC7rb77G%2BYPJrc0f6PGfy
 igJNHf%2FGj9KMQ3sIXZg%3D&reserved=0> for details.\n\nThat’s all for this
  week.  Please stay warm!\n\nBest regards\,\n\nVivek\n\nPS -- I’d like t
