 _______________________________________________________________\nFrom: F
 aculty <faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.e
 du>> On Behalf Of Sarkar\, Vivek\nSent: Wednesday\, February 19\, 2025 1
 :53 PM\nTo: Faculty@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Faculty@cc.gatech.edu>\; Staff@
 cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Staff@cc.gatech.edu>\; phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.e
 du<mailto:phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.ed
 u<mailto:ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu
 <mailto:cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu>\nSubject: [Faculty] Dean's Dispa
 tch – new committees for changing times\, kudos\n\nDear GT Computing com
 munity\,\n\nMany things are changing right now\, sometimes on a daily ba
 sis.  I know this can be stressful for everyone.  As I mentioned during 
 the listening sessions\, our greatest strength is our people. We are luc
 ky to have talented\, dedicated individuals who make ours a truly vibran
 t community.  This is very much a time for all of us to come together an
 d express kindness and compassion for everyone\, especially those who ar
 e the most vulnerable.  And be sure to extend kindness to yourself as we
 ll. No matter what the future brings\, we will face it together as a com
 munity.\n\nTo keep communication channels active\, I am also scheduling 
 weekly virtual office hours with the Dean for all CoC faculty\, staff\, 
 and students who would like to discuss any aspect of recent events and t
 heir potential impacts.  These will be held during 11:30am - 12:30pm on 
 Thursdays\, starting tomorrow (Feb 20th).  Please look out for a calenda
 r invitation and contact Cynthia Bryant (cebryant@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:c
 ebryant@cc.gatech.edu>) if you don’t see one.\n\nIn addition to the list
 ening sessions\, I very much appreciated meeting with our college adviso
 ry board members last Friday.  We are lucky to have such a talented and 
 experienced group of experts on our advisory board who care deeply about
  our college and are ready to share their advice and support in every wa
 y that they can.  It was very helpful to hear their perspectives\, and I
  look forward to further discussions during our upcoming advisory board 
 meeting on April 3-4.\n\nIn other news\, I am pleased to announce that M
 elinda McDaniel is the new interim Associate Chair of the School of Comp
 uting Instruction. Melinda is a GT alumna and has a decade of experience
  teaching our undergraduates --- we are lucky to have her in this leader
 ship position.  Many thanks to Melinda for stepping up this important ro
 le for SCI and the college!\n\nI'd also like to share updates on the two
  committees mentioned in last week's dispatch.  Both committees will wel
 come getting input from all of you\, of course.\n\nCoC Contingency Plann
 ing Committee\nThis committee includes representation from faculty\, sta
 ff\, and students. Its scope will include staying abreast of recent deve
 lopments\, identifying scenarios that need contingency planning\, and re
 commending contingency efforts for those scenarios.  It includes the fol
 lowing members:\n\n  *   Greg Eisenhauer (Senior Research Scientist\, SC
 S)\n  *   Ada Gavrilovska (Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Neha Kumar (Associate
  Professor\, IC)\n  *   Kim Macleod (Associate Director of Enterprise Se
 rvices\, TSO)\n  *   Melinda McDaniel (Senior Lecturer\, SCI)\n  *   Pet
 er Swire (J.Z. Liang Professor\, SCP and Scheller)\n  *   Xiuwei Zhang (
 J.Z. Liang Early-Career Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n\nWe are still waiti
 ng on confirming the student member of this committee and will announce 
 their name when it is confirmed.\n\nCoC Task Force on New Strategies for
  Funding Computing Research\nThis task force will be in charge of thinki
 ng strategically about exploring new ways to fund the research of CoC fa
 culty\, especially in areas that are vulnerable to loss of funding. It i
 ncludes the following members:\n\n  *   Carlos Batist (Assistant Directo
 r - Financial Operations\, SCS)\n  *   Tom Conte (Associate Dean for Res
 earch\, CoC\; and\, Professor\, SCS & ECE - Task Force Lead)\n  *   Albe
 rto Dainotti (Associate Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Munmun De Choudhury (Ass
 ociate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Rich DeMillo (Charlotte B. and Roger C. Wa
 rren Professor of Computing\, SCP)\n  *   Kristine Haskett (Executive Di
 rector Foundation Relations\, GT Office of Development)\n  *   Josiah He
 ster (Catherine M. and James E. Allchin Early Career Associate Professor
 \, IC)\n  *   Tamara Pearson (Senior Director\, Constellations Center\, 
 CoC)\n  *   Chao Zhang (Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n  *   Jason Zwang (S
 enior Director\, Development\, CoC)\n\nFinally\, I have kudos to share f
 or members of our community\, as always:\n\n  *   Our student Competitiv
 e Programming team has dominated in recent competitions.\n     *   Nearl
 y 100 Tech students took part in the Meta Hacker Cup\, with six students
  making it to the third round. Ph.D. candidate Sunghyeong Jo placed 8th 
 in the third round and was one of 500 to make it to the final round\, wh
 ere he placed 13th.\n     *   At the International Collegiate Programmin
 g Contest (ICPC) regionals\, Georgia Tech teams secured four of the top 
 10 spots. The top Georgia Tech team of Weiyu Chen\, Kevin Shan\, and Xie
 ting Chu solved all 13 problems\, placing second in the region and third
  nationally. Congratulations to all of the team members and to Abrahim L
 adha (SCI)\, their faculty advisor. Well done!\n\n  *   Our entrepreneur
 ial capstone course has more than doubled in size since we launched it i
 n 2023\, with a current enrollment of 126 students. In response\, the Co
 llege is expanding its course sections and deepening our relationship wi
 th CREATE-X\, the Institute’s entrepreneurship education initiative.  Se
 e the related story<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=
 https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-partnership-cre
 ate-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%4
 0gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7Cb70d8278bb8048dfd73c08de02782413%7C482198bbae
 7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638950912193231003%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZs
 b3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoi
 TWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=zsi40JMRg6%2FOPvcBYvYWHJ%2Bq
 nYZ6zb7Ggep9fFwsAys%3D&reserved=0> for details.\n\nThat’s all for this w
 eek.  Please stay warm!\n\nBest regards\,\n\nVivek\n\nPS -- I’d like to 
 remind everyone that our institute’s Spring Compliance Training is under
  way\, and that everyone in the college (including student employees) mu
 st complete it by February 28. I have completed it myself and can attest
  that it’s not too cumbersome … and it was interesting to see a module t
 here related to GenAI!\n\nStudent programming team: https://www.cc.gatec
 h.edu/news/competitive-programming-team-excels-major-competitions<https:
 //nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatec
