 ________________________________________________________________________
 _______\nFrom: Faculty <faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:faculty-bou
 nces@cc.gatech.edu>> On Behalf Of Sarkar\, Vivek\nSent: Wednesday\, Febr
 uary 19\, 2025 1:53 PM\nTo: Faculty@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Faculty@cc.gate
 ch.edu>\; Staff@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Staff@cc.gatech.edu>\; phd-coc-offi
 cial@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; ms-coc-offic
 ial@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; cocadvisoryboa
 rd@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu>\nSubject: [Facul
 ty] Dean's Dispatch – new committees for changing times\, kudos\n\nDear 
 GT Computing community\,\n\nMany things are changing right now\, sometim
 es on a daily basis.  I know this can be stressful for everyone.  As I m
 entioned during the listening sessions\, our greatest strength is our pe
 ople. We are lucky to have talented\, dedicated individuals who make our
 s a truly vibrant community.  This is very much a time for all of us to 
 come together and express kindness and compassion for everyone\, especia
 lly those who are the most vulnerable.  And be sure to extend kindness t
 o yourself as well. No matter what the future brings\, we will face it t
 ogether as a community.\n\nTo keep communication channels active\, I am 
 also scheduling weekly virtual office hours with the Dean for all CoC fa
 culty\, staff\, and students who would like to discuss any aspect of rec
 ent events and their potential impacts.  These will be held during 11:30
 am - 12:30pm on Thursdays\, starting tomorrow (Feb 20th).  Please look o
 ut for a calendar invitation and contact Cynthia Bryant (cebryant@cc.gat
 ech.edu<mailto:cebryant@cc.gatech.edu>) if you don’t see one.\n\nIn addi
 tion to the listening sessions\, I very much appreciated meeting with ou
 r college advisory board members last Friday.  We are lucky to have such
  a talented and experienced group of experts on our advisory board who c
 are deeply about our college and are ready to share their advice and sup
 port in every way that they can.  It was very helpful to hear their pers
 pectives\, and I look forward to further discussions during our upcoming
  advisory board meeting on April 3-4.\n\nIn other news\, I am pleased to
  announce that Melinda McDaniel is the new interim Associate Chair of th
 e School of Computing Instruction. Melinda is a GT alumna and has a deca
 de of experience teaching our undergraduates --- we are lucky to have he
 r in this leadership position.  Many thanks to Melinda for stepping up t
 his important role for SCI and the college!\n\nI'd also like to share up
 dates on the two committees mentioned in last week's dispatch.  Both com
 mittees will welcome getting input from all of you\, of course.\n\nCoC C
 ontingency Planning Committee\nThis committee includes representation fr
 om faculty\, staff\, and students. Its scope will include staying abreas
 t of recent developments\, identifying scenarios that need contingency p
 lanning\, and recommending contingency efforts for those scenarios.  It 
 includes the following members:\n\n  *   Greg Eisenhauer (Senior Researc
 h Scientist\, SCS)\n  *   Ada Gavrilovska (Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Neha 
 Kumar (Associate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Kim Macleod (Associate Director 
 of Enterprise Services\, TSO)\n  *   Melinda McDaniel (Senior Lecturer\,
  SCI)\n  *   Peter Swire (J.Z. Liang Professor\, SCP and Scheller)\n  * 
   Xiuwei Zhang (J.Z. Liang Early-Career Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n\nWe
  are still waiting on confirming the student member of this committee an
 d will announce their name when it is confirmed.\n\nCoC Task Force on Ne
 w Strategies for Funding Computing Research\nThis task force will be in 
 charge of thinking strategically about exploring new ways to fund the re
 search of CoC faculty\, especially in areas that are vulnerable to loss 
 of funding. It includes the following members:\n\n  *   Carlos Batist (A
 ssistant Director - Financial Operations\, SCS)\n  *   Tom Conte (Associ
 ate Dean for Research\, CoC\; and\, Professor\, SCS & ECE - Task Force L
 ead)\n  *   Alberto Dainotti (Associate Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Munmun D
 e Choudhury (Associate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Rich DeMillo (Charlotte B.
  and Roger C. Warren Professor of Computing\, SCP)\n  *   Kristine Haske
 tt (Executive Director Foundation Relations\, GT Office of Development)\
 n  *   Josiah Hester (Catherine M. and James E. Allchin Early Career Ass
 ociate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Tamara Pearson (Senior Director\, Constell
 ations Center\, CoC)\n  *   Chao Zhang (Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n  * 
   Jason Zwang (Senior Director\, Development\, CoC)\n\nFinally\, I have 
 kudos to share for members of our community\, as always:\n\n  *   Our st
 udent Competitive Programming team has dominated in recent competitions.
 \n     *   Nearly 100 Tech students took part in the Meta Hacker Cup\, w
 ith six students making it to the third round. Ph.D. candidate Sunghyeon
 g Jo placed 8th in the third round and was one of 500 to make it to the 
 final round\, where he placed 13th.\n     *   At the International Colle
 giate Programming Contest (ICPC) regionals\, Georgia Tech teams secured 
 four of the top 10 spots. The top Georgia Tech team of Weiyu Chen\, Kevi
 n Shan\, and Xieting Chu solved all 13 problems\, placing second in the 
 region and third nationally. Congratulations to all of the team members 
 and to Abrahim Ladha (SCI)\, their faculty advisor. Well done!\n\n  *   
 Our entrepreneurial capstone course has more than doubled in size since 
 we launched it in 2023\, with a current enrollment of 126 students. In r
 esponse\, the College is expanding its course sections and deepening our
  relationship with CREATE-X\, the Institute’s entrepreneurship education
  initiative.  See the related story<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.o
 utlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands
 -partnership-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C
 02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C29bcdbebec4743292ce808de0cb20
 2d2%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638962155886689035%7CUn
 known%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJX
 aW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=cY%2B5gcJH6b
 0DO1XW0bmh%2FZ8uBMrL0GM7781LXZj9QsE%3D&reserved=0> for details.\n\nThat’
 s all for this week.  Please stay warm!\n\nBest regards\,\n\nVivek\n\nPS
  -- I’d like to remind everyone that our institute’s Spring Compliance T
 raining is under way\, and that everyone in the college (including stude
 nt employees) must complete it by February 28. I have completed it mysel
 f and can attest that it’s not too cumbersome … and it was interesting t
 o see a module there related to GenAI!\n\nStudent programming team: http
 s://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/competitive-programming-team-excels-major-com
 petitions<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2
 F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcompetitive-programming-team-excels-major
 -competitions&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C29bcd
 bebec4743292ce808de0cb202d2%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7
 C638962155886704692%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYi
 OiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%
 7C%7C&sdata=yKmiO4u8YlFCFvz8ixy72mgqsk1%2F821U9MsbRRZT9EE%3D&reserved=0>
 \n\nExpanding its course selections and deepening our relationship with 
 CREATE-X: https://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/college-expands-partnership-cre
 ate-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum<https://nam12.safelinks.pr
 otection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcolle
 ge-expands-partnership-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&
 data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C29bcdbebec4743292ce
 808de0cb202d2%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C6389621558867
 18525%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMC
 IsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=%2
 FAHmwbLoOGYLRo8GolND7jNdzP7fugalgJDPmt4mCnk%3D&reserved=0>\n\n\nVivek Sa
 rkar<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fvs
 arkar.cc.gatech.edu%2F&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.co
 m%7C29bcdbebec4743292ce808de0cb202d2%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%
 7C1%7C0%7C638962155886732627%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnR
 ydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3
 D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=GoNG4tIgN53BuDUvKHG7GO3uL6DyWs%2FC8GHfOUW%2BlgI%3D&
 reserved=0>\nJohn P. Imlay Jr. Dean\, College of Computing\nGeorgia Inst
 itute of Technology\nEA: Cynthia Bryant\, cebryant@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:
 cebryant@cc.gatech.edu>\, 404-385-5661\n\n\n\nMy work hours might differ
  from yours\, so please don’t feel obligated to respond to my evening/we
 ekend/holiday emails until you are back at work.\n\n[cid:image001.jpg@01
 DB82E3.590FB3F0]\n\n
