 __________________\n\nFrom: Faculty <faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu<mailt
 o:faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu>> On Behalf Of Sarkar\, Vivek\nSent: Wed
 nesday\, February 19\, 2025 1:53 PM\nTo: Faculty@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Fa
 culty@cc.gatech.edu>\; Staff@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Staff@cc.gatech.edu>\;
  phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\;
  ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu>\; c
 ocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu>\nSu
 bject: [Faculty] Dean's Dispatch – new committees for changing times\, k
 udos\n\n\n\nDear GT Computing community\,\n\n\n\nMany things are changin
 g right now\, sometimes on a daily basis.  I know this can be stressful 
 for everyone.  As I mentioned during the listening sessions\, our greate
 st strength is our people. We are lucky to have talented\, dedicated ind
 ividuals who make ours a truly vibrant community.  This is very much a t
 ime for all of us to come together and express kindness and compassion f
 or everyone\, especially those who are the most vulnerable.  And be sure
  to extend kindness to yourself as well. No matter what the future bring
 s\, we will face it together as a community.\n\n\n\nTo keep communicatio
 n channels active\, I am also scheduling weekly virtual office hours wit
 h the Dean for all CoC faculty\, staff\, and students who would like to 
 discuss any aspect of recent events and their potential impacts.  These 
 will be held during 11:30am - 12:30pm on Thursdays\, starting tomorrow (
 Feb 20th).  Please look out for a calendar invitation and contact Cynthi
 a Bryant (cebryant@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cebryant@cc.gatech.edu>) if you 
 don’t see one.\n\n\n\nIn addition to the listening sessions\, I very muc
 h appreciated meeting with our college advisory board members last Frida
 y.  We are lucky to have such a talented and experienced group of expert
 s on our advisory board who care deeply about our college and are ready 
 to share their advice and support in every way that they can.  It was ve
 ry helpful to hear their perspectives\, and I look forward to further di
 scussions during our upcoming advisory board meeting on April 3-4.\n\n\n
 \nIn other news\, I am pleased to announce that Melinda McDaniel is the 
 new interim Associate Chair of the School of Computing Instruction. Meli
 nda is a GT alumna and has a decade of experience teaching our undergrad
 uates --- we are lucky to have her in this leadership position.  Many th
 anks to Melinda for stepping up this important role for SCI and the coll
 ege!\n\n\n\nI'd also like to share updates on the two committees mention
 ed in last week's dispatch.  Both committees will welcome getting input 
 from all of you\, of course.\n\n\n\nCoC Contingency Planning Committee\n
 \nThis committee includes representation from faculty\, staff\, and stud
 ents. Its scope will include staying abreast of recent developments\, id
 entifying scenarios that need contingency planning\, and recommending co
 ntingency efforts for those scenarios.  It includes the following member
 s:\n\n  *   Greg Eisenhauer (Senior Research Scientist\, SCS)\n  *   Ada
  Gavrilovska (Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Neha Kumar (Associate Professor\, 
 IC)\n  *   Kim Macleod (Associate Director of Enterprise Services\, TSO)
 \n  *   Melinda McDaniel (Senior Lecturer\, SCI)\n  *   Peter Swire (J.Z
 . Liang Professor\, SCP and Scheller)\n  *   Xiuwei Zhang (J.Z. Liang Ea
 rly-Career Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n\n\n\nWe are still waiting on con
 firming the student member of this committee and will announce their nam
 e when it is confirmed.\n\n\n\nCoC Task Force on New Strategies for Fund
 ing Computing Research\n\nThis task force will be in charge of thinking 
 strategically about exploring new ways to fund the research of CoC facul
 ty\, especially in areas that are vulnerable to loss of funding. It incl
 udes the following members:\n\n  *   Carlos Batist (Assistant Director -
  Financial Operations\, SCS)\n  *   Tom Conte (Associate Dean for Resear
 ch\, CoC\; and\, Professor\, SCS & ECE - Task Force Lead)\n  *   Alberto
  Dainotti (Associate Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Munmun De Choudhury (Associ
 ate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Rich DeMillo (Charlotte B. and Roger C. Warre
 n Professor of Computing\, SCP)\n  *   Kristine Haskett (Executive Direc
 tor Foundation Relations\, GT Office of Development)\n  *   Josiah Heste
 r (Catherine M. and James E. Allchin Early Career Associate Professor\, 
 IC)\n  *   Tamara Pearson (Senior Director\, Constellations Center\, CoC
 )\n  *   Chao Zhang (Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n  *   Jason Zwang (Seni
 or Director\, Development\, CoC)\n\n\n\nFinally\, I have kudos to share 
 for members of our community\, as always:\n\n  *   Our student Competiti
 ve Programming team has dominated in recent competitions.\n     *   Near
 ly 100 Tech students took part in the Meta Hacker Cup\, with six student
 s making it to the third round. Ph.D. candidate Sunghyeong Jo placed 8th
  in the third round and was one of 500 to make it to the final round\, w
 here he placed 13th.\n     *   At the International Collegiate Programmi
 ng Contest (ICPC) regionals\, Georgia Tech teams secured four of the top
  10 spots. The top Georgia Tech team of Weiyu Chen\, Kevin Shan\, and Xi
 eting Chu solved all 13 problems\, placing second in the region and thir
 d nationally. Congratulations to all of the team members and to Abrahim 
 Ladha (SCI)\, their faculty advisor. Well done!\n  *   Our entrepreneuri
 al capstone course has more than doubled in size since we launched it in
  2023\, with a current enrollment of 126 students. In response\, the Col
 lege is expanding its course sections and deepening our relationship wit
 h CREATE-X\, the Institute’s entrepreneurship education initiative.  See
  the related story<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=h
 ttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-partnership-crea
 te-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40
 gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C1078e0a9b4bd412373ea08de2928dfa2%7C482198bbae7
 b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638993452716307501%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb
 3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiT
 WFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=yO6KGT9X0ernT8F91mV%2B8Lm%2Bg
 S1T1ncjMAMhkI6DqGI%3D&reserved=0> for details.\n\n\n\nThat’s all for thi
 s week.  Please stay warm!\n\n\n\nBest regards\,\n\n\n\nVivek\n\n\n\nPS 
 -- I’d like to remind everyone that our institute’s Spring Compliance Tr
 aining is under way\, and that everyone in the college (including studen
 t employees) must complete it by February 28. I have completed it myself
  and can attest that it’s not too cumbersome … and it was interesting to
  see a module there related to GenAI!\n\n\n\nStudent programming team: h
 ttps://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/competitive-programming-team-excels-major-
 competitions<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3
 A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcompetitive-programming-team-excels-ma
 jor-competitions&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C10
 78e0a9b4bd412373ea08de2928dfa2%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C
 0%7C638993452716323082%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsI
 lYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%
 7C%7C%7C&sdata=njCtYujh%2BtB42l1Jw5X8ntDIWALRZY9MOfZa8HAyYfc%3D&reserved
 =0>\n\n\n\nExpanding its course selections and deepening our relationshi
 p with CREATE-X: https://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/college-expands-partners
 hip-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum<https://nam12.safel
