 _______________________________\n\nFrom: Faculty <faculty-bounces@cc.gat
 ech.edu<mailto:faculty-bounces@cc.gatech.edu>> On Behalf Of Sarkar\, Viv
 ek\nSent: Wednesday\, February 19\, 2025 1:53 PM\nTo: Faculty@cc.gatech.
 edu<mailto:Faculty@cc.gatech.edu>\; Staff@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:Staff@cc.
 gatech.edu>\; phd-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:phd-coc-official@cc.
 gatech.edu>\; ms-coc-official@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:ms-coc-official@cc.ga
 tech.edu>\; cocadvisoryboard@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cocadvisoryboard@cc.ga
 tech.edu>\nSubject: [Faculty] Dean's Dispatch – new committees for chang
 ing times\, kudos\n\n\n\nDear GT Computing community\,\n\n\n\nMany thing
 s are changing right now\, sometimes on a daily basis.  I know this can 
 be stressful for everyone.  As I mentioned during the listening sessions
 \, our greatest strength is our people. We are lucky to have talented\, 
 dedicated individuals who make ours a truly vibrant community.  This is 
 very much a time for all of us to come together and express kindness and
  compassion for everyone\, especially those who are the most vulnerable.
   And be sure to extend kindness to yourself as well. No matter what the
  future brings\, we will face it together as a community.\n\n\n\nTo keep
  communication channels active\, I am also scheduling weekly virtual off
 ice hours with the Dean for all CoC faculty\, staff\, and students who w
 ould like to discuss any aspect of recent events and their potential imp
 acts.  These will be held during 11:30am - 12:30pm on Thursdays\, starti
 ng tomorrow (Feb 20th).  Please look out for a calendar invitation and c
 ontact Cynthia Bryant (cebryant@cc.gatech.edu<mailto:cebryant@cc.gatech.
 edu>) if you don’t see one.\n\n\n\nIn addition to the listening sessions
 \, I very much appreciated meeting with our college advisory board membe
 rs last Friday.  We are lucky to have such a talented and experienced gr
 oup of experts on our advisory board who care deeply about our college a
 nd are ready to share their advice and support in every way that they ca
 n.  It was very helpful to hear their perspectives\, and I look forward 
 to further discussions during our upcoming advisory board meeting on Apr
 il 3-4.\n\n\n\nIn other news\, I am pleased to announce that Melinda McD
 aniel is the new interim Associate Chair of the School of Computing Inst
 ruction. Melinda is a GT alumna and has a decade of experience teaching 
 our undergraduates --- we are lucky to have her in this leadership posit
 ion.  Many thanks to Melinda for stepping up this important role for SCI
  and the college!\n\n\n\nI'd also like to share updates on the two commi
 ttees mentioned in last week's dispatch.  Both committees will welcome g
 etting input from all of you\, of course.\n\n\n\nCoC Contingency Plannin
 g Committee\n\nThis committee includes representation from faculty\, sta
 ff\, and students. Its scope will include staying abreast of recent deve
 lopments\, identifying scenarios that need contingency planning\, and re
 commending contingency efforts for those scenarios.  It includes the fol
 lowing members:\n\n  *   Greg Eisenhauer (Senior Research Scientist\, SC
 S)\n  *   Ada Gavrilovska (Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Neha Kumar (Associate
  Professor\, IC)\n  *   Kim Macleod (Associate Director of Enterprise Se
 rvices\, TSO)\n  *   Melinda McDaniel (Senior Lecturer\, SCI)\n  *   Pet
 er Swire (J.Z. Liang Professor\, SCP and Scheller)\n  *   Xiuwei Zhang (
 J.Z. Liang Early-Career Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n\n\n\nWe are still w
 aiting on confirming the student member of this committee and will annou
 nce their name when it is confirmed.\n\n\n\nCoC Task Force on New Strate
 gies for Funding Computing Research\n\nThis task force will be in charge
  of thinking strategically about exploring new ways to fund the research
  of CoC faculty\, especially in areas that are vulnerable to loss of fun
 ding. It includes the following members:\n\n  *   Carlos Batist (Assista
 nt Director - Financial Operations\, SCS)\n  *   Tom Conte (Associate De
 an for Research\, CoC\; and\, Professor\, SCS & ECE - Task Force Lead)\n
   *   Alberto Dainotti (Associate Professor\, SCS)\n  *   Munmun De Chou
 dhury (Associate Professor\, IC)\n  *   Rich DeMillo (Charlotte B. and R
 oger C. Warren Professor of Computing\, SCP)\n  *   Kristine Haskett (Ex
 ecutive Director Foundation Relations\, GT Office of Development)\n  *  
  Josiah Hester (Catherine M. and James E. Allchin Early Career Associate
  Professor\, IC)\n  *   Tamara Pearson (Senior Director\, Constellations
  Center\, CoC)\n  *   Chao Zhang (Assistant Professor\, CSE)\n  *   Jaso
 n Zwang (Senior Director\, Development\, CoC)\n\n\n\nFinally\, I have ku
 dos to share for members of our community\, as always:\n\n  *   Our stud
 ent Competitive Programming team has dominated in recent competitions.\n
      *   Nearly 100 Tech students took part in the Meta Hacker Cup\, wit
 h six students making it to the third round. Ph.D. candidate Sunghyeong 
 Jo placed 8th in the third round and was one of 500 to make it to the fi
 nal round\, where he placed 13th.\n     *   At the International Collegi
 ate Programming Contest (ICPC) regionals\, Georgia Tech teams secured fo
 ur of the top 10 spots. The top Georgia Tech team of Weiyu Chen\, Kevin 
 Shan\, and Xieting Chu solved all 13 problems\, placing second in the re
 gion and third nationally. Congratulations to all of the team members an
 d to Abrahim Ladha (SCI)\, their faculty advisor. Well done!\n  *   Our 
 entrepreneurial capstone course has more than doubled in size since we l
 aunched it in 2023\, with a current enrollment of 126 students. In respo
 nse\, the College is expanding its course sections and deepening our rel
 ationship with CREATE-X\, the Institute’s entrepreneurship education ini
 tiative.  See the related story<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlo
 ok.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-par
 tnership-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7
 Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft.com%7C9ee3df4f209549dd85c508de292820c9%
 7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638993449504409810%7CUnknow
 n%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4z
 MiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=QN6xjes0RfSQtCP%
 2BjXEKT50eAU3Glx5dr6VU0Mc4%2FW8%3D&reserved=0> for details.\n\n\n\nThat’
 s all for this week.  Please stay warm!\n\n\n\nBest regards\,\n\n\n\nViv
 ek\n\n\n\nPS -- I’d like to remind everyone that our institute’s Spring 
 Compliance Training is under way\, and that everyone in the college (inc
 luding student employees) must complete it by February 28. I have comple
 ted it myself and can attest that it’s not too cumbersome … and it was i
 nteresting to see a module there related to GenAI!\n\n\n\nStudent progra
 mming team: https://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/competitive-programming-team-
 excels-major-competitions<https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com
 /?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc.gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcompetitive-programming-t
 eam-excels-major-competitions&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicro
 soft.com%7C9ee3df4f209549dd85c508de292820c9%7C482198bbae7b4b258b7a6d7f32
 faa083%7C1%7C0%7C638993449504430939%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1h
 cGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDAwMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoy
 fQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=%2Fq%2BctfXcIYtS%2FZKKQKER%2BSMD4P9RLE52TOUY
 jvqMdDA%3D&reserved=0>\n\n\n\nExpanding its course selections and deepen
 ing our relationship with CREATE-X: https://www.cc.gatech.edu/news/colle
 ge-expands-partnership-create-x-double-down-entrepreneurship-curriculum<
 https://nam12.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.cc
 .gatech.edu%2Fnews%2Fcollege-expands-partnership-create-x-double-down-en
 trepreneurship-curriculum&data=05%7C02%7Crzhang662%40gtvault.onmicrosoft
