ATTENDEE;CN="Choi, Youngsoo";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="choi15@llnl.gov";P
 ARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;ROLE=CHAIR:mailto:choi15@llnl.gov
ATTENDEE;CN="Data Driven Physics Simulation";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="dd
 ps@llnl.gov";ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT:mailto:ddps@llnl.gov
ATTENDEE;CN="Youngjoon Hong";CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;EMAIL="hongyj@snu.ac.kr";
 ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT:mailto:hongyj@snu.ac.kr
CREATED:20260125T225046Z
DESCRIPTION:We will host Youngjoon Hong (Seoul National University\, htt
 ps://www.youngjoonhong.com/videos) as a DDPS seminar speaker. Hope to se
 e you many of you at the seminar:\n\n\nOperator Networks Based on Numeri
 cal Analysis\n\nYoungjoon Hong\n\nSeoul National University\n\nThursday\
 , February 20\, 2025\n4:00 PM\nWebEx\n\n\nAbstract: We propose a novel a
 pproach for solving parametric partial differential equations (PDEs) usi
 ng an operator network. This method combines the strengths of deep learn
 ing with traditional numerical techniques\, specifically the finite elem
 ent or spectral element methods\, to address parametric PDEs ranging fro
 m singularly perturbed convection-diffusion equations to the Navier-Stok
 es equations\, all without requiring paired input-output training data. 
 Through extensive experiments on various benchmark problems\, our approa
 ch has demonstrated excellent performance across diverse settings\, show
 casing its versatility in terms of accuracy\, generalization\, and compu
 tational efficiency. The proposed framework holds significant potential 
 for applications in fields where PDEs are critical for modeling complex 
 domains with diverse boundary conditions and singular behavior. Addition
 ally\, we provide a rigorous theoretical convergence analysis\, grounded
  in numerical analysis\, to further support our approach.\n\nBio: As an 
 Associate Professor at Seoul National University\, Youngjoon Hong focuse
 s his research on the mathematics of machine learning and its applicatio
 ns in scientific computing. He earned his Ph.D. in Mathematics with a mi
 nor in Scientific Computing from Indiana University under the guidance o
 f Professor Roger Temam\, where he developed a strong foundation in theo
 retical analysis and computational techniques. During his postdoctoral w
 ork at the University of Illinois at Chicago with Professors Jerry Bona 
 and David Nicholls\, he conducted research on electromagnetic and water 
 waves\, further honing his problem-solving skills. He later initiated in
 dependent studies on the use of neural networks in scientific research\,
  leading to a focused research program at San Diego State University\, w
 here he began investigating neural network approximation within scientif
 ic machine learning. Currently\, his work is dedicated to developing the
 oretical frameworks that enhance the reliability and applicability of ne
 ural networks in addressing complex scientific and engineering challenge
 s.\n\n\n📚 DDPS seminar is organized by libROM team ( www.librom.net<htt
 p://www.librom.net> ).\n🗓️ DDPS seminar schedule: https://www.librom.ne
 t/ddps.html<https://www.youtube.com/redirect?event=video_description&red
 ir_token=QUFFLUhqblRkS256NDFhdjRyNHpRRFYwSm5jT0t0MVNvZ3xBQ3Jtc0treERKS1B
 uSkhPd3FHaXFqRDZPUnZtRjh1b01WcjJuczBSZFA1aGRranNtOVNFNlpONmxHSkRHLUZEeVA
 5Y24wVXRHRi1wdGdDT3E5RlFneHFVdUpNTk1KeEIwNjMzLTBTVjZueDRodXp0c2VLWTZDUQ&
 q=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.librom.net%2Fddps.html&v=uksMn36aecg>\n💻 LLNL News:
  https://www.llnl.gov/news<https://www.youtube.com/redirect?event=video_
 description&redir_token=QUFFLUhqa2RhQlRlU3N0QThpOFhfeFJhclpSd0RRRkFGd3xB
 Q3Jtc0trdlZna1FQcmQtVG1CQ3VOUVoxekpPalR4ZlFUdjRXSmtJSEFmM3NacmJOSnA2M3dn
